<GuidePageShell
  slug="how-much-to-feed-a-puppy"
  title="How Much to Feed a Puppy: Calories & Meals"
  description="Practical puppy feeding guide covering calories, meal frequency, and common overfeeding mistakes, with a calculator."
  answer="Most puppies need about two to three times the resting energy of an adult dog: roughly 3 × RER under four months and 2 × RER afterward, spread over three or four meals a day. Start with the calculator or the bag’s chart, then adjust based on your puppy’s body condition."
